Regarding AI security controls, we have implemented measures to protect against prompt injection, output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and confidence threshold escalation. Model isolation is ensured through an inference API with no direct model access for end users, and model updates undergo a security review.

For audit capabilities, all queries are logged, and log immutability is maintained through append-only logging with SHA-256 hash chaining. Audit logs are retained for 7 years, and we have the capability to export logs in a format compatible with CNIL requirements. Real-time SIEM integration is also available using tools like Wazuh and Elastic SIEM.

To ensure explicability and transparency of recommendations and proposals, our AI systems can be designed to provide explanations for their outputs, though specific details on this capability are not provided in my current context. 

Given these measures, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. appears well-positioned to meet the client's demands regarding GDPR compliance, data protection, and AI security controls, while also providing necessary audit capabilities.
