2026-06-01 15:12:01,493 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-06-01 15:12:01,494 | AGENT | CSRSustainability Agent answered: Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l., can contribute to the City of Belval's sustainability goals by incorporating several key elements into the proposed solution. Firstly, we can apply digital sobriety practices such as INT8/INT4 model quantisation to reduce GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching to reduce recomputes by an estimated 20%, and implementing a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum 5-year lifecycle. 

Additionally, we can leverage our partnership with green hosting providers like OVHcloud and Scaleway, both of which are located in France, use 100% renewable energy, and have ISO14001 certification, ensuring low-carbon-impact infrastructures. Our typical energy reduction versus baseline is around 35%, which aligns well with reducing energetic consumption.

From a social commitment perspective, we prioritize gender equality with an index score of 88, employ disabled workers at a rate of 4.2%, prefer local subcontracting, adhere to accessibility standards such as WCAG 2.1 AA and RGAA 4.1, and provide 42 hours of training per employee per year.

To ensure AI ethics principles are upheld, we have published an ethics charter that mandates human oversight for all AI recommendations, ensures no discriminatory outputs through quarterly bias testing, provides transparency of data sources to end users, and grants the right to contest any AI-generated suggestion. Quarterly bias audits are conducted, and a whistleblowing policy is in place.

By integrating these practices and commitments into our proposed solution, we can effectively contribute to reducing energetic consumption, utilizing low-carbon-impact infrastructures, and upholding AI ethics principles, thus supporting the City of Belval's environmental footprint reduction goals.
