2026-06-01 15:13:33,436 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: # 1. Executive Summary
The City of Belval has issued a call for tenders to implement an artificial intelligence solution that assists municipal agents in their daily tasks, enhancing efficiency and service quality. Our consortium, led by Nexus Engineering S.r.l., proposes a comprehensive solution integrating AI innovation, sovereign cloud hosting, green IT practices, and strict GDPR compliance. This proposal outlines our approach, detailing the technical architecture, security measures, legal compliance, budget considerations, AI capabilities, and sustainability commitments.

# 2. Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval requires an AI solution that assists agents with information search, drafting help, and file instruction assistance, all while ensuring GDPR compliance, explicability, transparency, and no automated decisions without agent validation. The solution must integrate with existing systems, provide fast response times (<2 seconds), guarantee high availability (99.9%), and be hosted on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU.

# 3. Proposed Solution
Our consortium proposes a microservices architecture with containerized services deployed on a Kubernetes cluster hosted on Outscale (SecNumCloud) infrastructure. This ensures scalability, high availability, and fast response times. For AI capabilities, we will utilize our sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, fine-tuned using LoRA or QLoRA methods to adapt to the client's domain and tone. Our RAG capabilities, employing dense vector semantic retrieval or hybrid strategies, will facilitate precise information search and retrieval.

To ensure explicability and transparency, we will implement source citation through RAG grounding, display chain-of-thought rationales, and utilize SHAP or LIME for model interpretability. Confidence scoring will be integrated to identify low-confidence responses, triggering an uncertainty warning and escalating the query to a human supervisor if necessary.

For security and compliance, we leverage our existing GDPR compliance posture, with standard data residency in the EU only and no cross-border transfers without explicit legal basis. We utilize anonymisation tools like Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models for protecting sensitive data. Our AI security controls include measures against prompt injection, output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and confidence threshold escalation.

From a legal perspective, we are compliant with required standard contractual clauses, including a sla penalty mechanism, termination for cause and convenience notices, data return on termination, and a data destruction certificate. Our insurance coverage includes professional indemnity, cyber liability, and we have a performance bond capacity.

Our budget proposal aims to achieve a gross margin of 28%, implying a gross profit of approximately €840,000 over the 4-year project duration, with an annual cost of exploitation mastered and compatible with the City's budgetary capacities. To optimize costs, we will focus on efficient resource allocation, renegotiating rates with subcontractors if necessary, and streamlining project management processes.

In terms of sustainability, we commit to reducing energetic consumption by applying digital sobriety practices such as INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and implementing a green IT hardware procurement policy. Our partnership with OVHcloud and Scaleway ensures low-carbon-impact infrastructures. We prioritize gender equality, employ disabled workers, prefer local subcontracting, adhere to accessibility standards, and provide extensive employee training.

# 4. Unaddressed Requirements
No requirements from the tender were left unaddressed by our consortium's proposal. Each aspect of the call for tenders has been carefully considered and incorporated into our comprehensive solution.

# 5. Conclusion
Our consortium's proposal offers a holistic solution that meets all the requirements outlined in the City of Belval's call for tenders. By combining cutting-edge AI technology with strict GDPR compliance, sovereign cloud hosting, green IT practices, and a commitment to sustainability, we are confident that our solution will significantly enhance the efficiency and quality of municipal services. We look forward to the opportunity to collaborate with the City of Belval in achieving its digital transformation goals.
